{"slug":"routes-with-few-turns","title":"Count the Routes That Turn at Most k Times","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":764,"tags":["dp","grid","counting","direction-state"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Remember the last direction and the number of turns used so far","body":["A robot walks from the top left cell to the bottom right cell of a grid with walls, moving **right or down**. A *turn* is a move whose direction differs from the previous move (the first move is never a turn). How many routes have **at most `k` turns**? For a free 3 by 3 grid and `k = 1` there are 2 routes (right, right, down, down and down, down, right, right); with `k = 2` there are 4 (all 6 routes have at most 3 turns). Print the count modulo 1 000 000 007.","The count of routes to a cell is not enough, because a new move is a turn or not depending on **how the robot arrived**. So the state is `(cell, last direction, turns used)`. Let `f(i, j, d, t)` be the number of routes to the cell `(i, j)` whose last move had the direction `d` (0 = right, 1 = down) and that used exactly `t` turns. A route that arrives in `(i, j)` moving right came from `(i, j - 1)`: if its last move was also right, the turns are the same; if its last move was down, this move is a turn, so it had `t - 1` turns. Moving down is symmetric. The cells next to the start get one route without any turn.",{"code":"for i in range(h):\n    for j in range(w):\n        if wall[i][j]: continue\n        for t in range(k + 1):\n            # arrive moving right, from the left cell\n            f[i][j][0][t] = f[i][j-1][0][t] + (f[i][j-1][1][t-1] if t >= 1 else 0)\n            # arrive moving down, from the cell above\n            f[i][j][1][t] = f[i-1][j][1][t] + (f[i-1][j][0][t-1] if t >= 1 else 0)\n# (the first move out of the start is added by hand: it has no turn)\nanswer = sum(f[h-1][w-1][d][t] for d in (0, 1) for t in range(k + 1))"},"Adding \"what we need to remember about the past\" to the state is the key: here the last direction (2 values) and the number of turns (up to `k + 1` values), so there are `h * w * 2 * (k + 1)` states, at most 223 000. Each state takes O(1) time. The same method handles limits on the number of turns, of changes, of walls broken, or of any small counter."]},"statement":["A grid has `h` rows and `w` columns; `.` is a free cell and `#` is a wall. A robot starts in the top left cell and moves one cell right or down at a time, never entering a wall, until it reaches the bottom right cell. A turn is a move whose direction differs from the previous move. Print the number of routes with at most `k` turns, modulo 1000000007. (If the grid is a single cell, there is one route with no turns.)"],"inputFormat":["The first line has `h`, `w` and `k`.","Each of the next `h` lines has a row of `w` characters: `.` is a free cell and `#` is a wall."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of routes modulo 1000000007."],"constraints":["1 <= h, w <= 60","0 <= k <= 30","The top left and the bottom right cells are free."],"examples":[{"input":"3 3 1\n...\n...\n...\n","output":"2\n","note":"Only the routes right-right-down-down and down-down-right-right have at most one turn: 2."},{"input":"2 2 0\n..\n..\n","output":"0\n","note":"Every route in a 2 by 2 grid has one turn: 0."}],"hints":["The state is the cell, the direction of the last move and the number of turns used.","Arriving in the same direction as the previous move keeps the turns; arriving in the other direction adds one turn.","The first move from the start is not a turn."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nh, w, k = map(int, input().split())\ngrid = [input().strip() for _ in range(h)]\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <array>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long h;\n    long long w;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> h >> w >> k;\n    vector<string> grid(h);\n    for (int i = 0; i < h; i++) {\n        cin >> grid[i];\n    }\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long h = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long w = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long k = Long.parseLong(next());\n        String[] grid = new String[(int) h];\n        for (int i = 0; i < grid.length; i++) {\n            grid[i] = next();\n        }\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["f(i, j, d, t) is the number of routes to the cell (i, j) whose last move had the direction d and that used exactly t turns; arriving in the direction of the previous move keeps t, arriving in the other direction needs t - 1 turns before. The answer is the sum of the values of the last cell for t up to k."],"complexity":"Time O(h * w * k), space O(h * w * k).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nh, w, k = map(int, input().split())\ngrid = [input().strip() for _ in range(h)]\n\nMOD = 10 ** 9 + 7\nT = k + 1\nf = [[[[0] * T for _ in range(2)] for _ in range(w)] for _ in range(h)]\nif h == 1 and w == 1:\n    print(1)\nelse:\n    for i in range(h):\n        for j in range(w):\n            if grid[i][j] == \"#\" or (i == 0 and j == 0):\n                continue\n            cell = f[i][j]\n            if j > 0 and grid[i][j - 1] != \"#\":\n                if i == 0 and j == 1:\n                    cell[0][0] += 1\n                else:\n                    left = f[i][j - 1]\n                    for t in range(T):\n                        v = left[0][t] + (left[1][t - 1] if t >= 1 else 0)\n                        cell[0][t] = (cell[0][t] + v) % MOD\n            if i > 0 and grid[i - 1][j] != \"#\":\n                if i == 1 and j == 0:\n                    cell[1][0] += 1\n                else:\n                    up = f[i - 1][j]\n                    for t in range(T):\n                        v = up[1][t] + (up[0][t - 1] if t >= 1 else 0)\n                        cell[1][t] = (cell[1][t] + v) % MOD\n    end = f[h - 1][w - 1]\n    print((sum(end[0]) + sum(end[1])) % MOD)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <array>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long h;\n    long long w;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> h >> w >> k;\n    vector<string> grid(h);\n    for (int i = 0; i < h; i++) {\n        cin >> grid[i];\n    }\n\n    const long long MOD = 1000000007;\n    int T = (int)k + 1;\n    vector<vector<array<vector<long long>, 2>>> f(h, vector<array<vector<long long>, 2>>(w));\n    for (int i = 0; i < h; i++) for (int j = 0; j < w; j++) { f[i][j][0].assign(T, 0); f[i][j][1].assign(T, 0); }\n    if (h == 1 && w == 1) {\n        cout << 1 << \"\\n\";\n    } else {\n        for (int i = 0; i < h; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < w; j++) {\n                if (grid[i][j] == '#' || (i == 0 && j == 0)) continue;\n                if (j > 0 && grid[i][j - 1] != '#') {\n                    if (i == 0 && j == 1) {\n                        f[i][j][0][0] += 1;\n                    } else {\n                        for (int t = 0; t < T; t++) {\n                            long long v = f[i][j - 1][0][t] + (t >= 1 ? f[i][j - 1][1][t - 1] : 0);\n                            f[i][j][0][t] = (f[i][j][0][t] + v) % MOD;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                if (i > 0 && grid[i - 1][j] != '#') {\n                    if (i == 1 && j == 0) {\n                        f[i][j][1][0] += 1;\n                    } else {\n                        for (int t = 0; t < T; t++) {\n                            long long v = f[i - 1][j][1][t] + (t >= 1 ? f[i - 1][j][0][t - 1] : 0);\n                            f[i][j][1][t] = (f[i][j][1][t] + v) % MOD;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        long long total = 0;\n        for (int t = 0; t < T; t++) total += f[h - 1][w - 1][0][t] + f[h - 1][w - 1][1][t];\n        cout << total % MOD << \"\\n\";\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long h = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long w = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long k = Long.parseLong(next());\n        String[] grid = new String[(int) h];\n        for (int i = 0; i < grid.length; i++) {\n            grid[i] = next();\n        }\n\n        final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n        int rowsCount = (int) h, colsCount = (int) w, T = (int) k + 1;\n        if (rowsCount == 1 && colsCount == 1) {\n            System.out.println(1);\n        } else {\n            long[][][][] f = new long[rowsCount][colsCount][2][T];\n            for (int i = 0; i < rowsCount; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < colsCount; j++) {\n                    if (grid[i].charAt(j) == '#' || (i == 0 && j == 0)) continue;\n                    if (j > 0 && grid[i].charAt(j - 1) != '#') {\n                        if (i == 0 && j == 1) {\n                            f[i][j][0][0] += 1;\n                        } else {\n                            for (int t = 0; t < T; t++) {\n                                long v = f[i][j - 1][0][t] + (t >= 1 ? f[i][j - 1][1][t - 1] : 0);\n                                f[i][j][0][t] = (f[i][j][0][t] + v) % MOD;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                    if (i > 0 && grid[i - 1].charAt(j) != '#') {\n                        if (i == 1 && j == 0) {\n                            f[i][j][1][0] += 1;\n                        } else {\n                            for (int t = 0; t < T; t++) {\n                                long v = f[i - 1][j][1][t] + (t >= 1 ? f[i - 1][j][0][t - 1] : 0);\n                                f[i][j][1][t] = (f[i][j][1][t] + v) % MOD;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            long total = 0;\n            for (int t = 0; t < T; t++) total += f[rowsCount - 1][colsCount - 1][0][t] + f[rowsCount - 1][colsCount - 1][1][t];\n            System.out.println(total % MOD);\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"3 3 1\n...\n...\n...\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"2 2 0\n..\n..\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"1 1 0\n.\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"1 5 0\n.....\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"3 1 0\n.\n.\n.\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"10 10 3\n..#...#...\n#.........\n......#...\n.......#..\n.#...#.#..\n.#........\n.....#..##\n..........\n..........\n...#......\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"30 30 10\n.............#.............#..\n......#....#.........#........\n..#.........#................#\n..............................\n.........#........#.........#.\n...#...........#..............\n...................#.#........\n...........#..................\n............#.........#.......\n...................#..........\n.................#.#..........\n..#................##.........\n...................#..........\n..............................\n........................#..#..\n#......